On 2009-12-01, Borek Lupom??sk� <borek.lupomesky@gmail.com> wrote:
> I stepped into a hidden room with "ad aerarium" written in front of
> it; and instead of being teleported to a vault it teleported me to
> dlvl 1! How can this be?

It happens: both vault teleporters and level teleporters can be marked
with the same message, although niches with level teleporters can only
be generated below dlvl 15, IIRC.

As I understand it, it's a bad Latin pun: _aerarium_ means "treasury",
derived from _aes_ ("copper", "money"); but Latin also has the word
_aer_ ("air"), which conjugates similarly and could be used to derive
the word _aerarium_ in the sense of "airy place", "sky".  So the trap
in the niche might send you either to a vault or up into the sky, so
to speak.  (Of course, you won't actually end up in the sky unless you
have teleport control and choose to teleport to a negative level.)

(Disclaimer: I don't actually know more than the faintest traces of
Latin grammar, so anything I've said above related to it should be
taken with a very large grain of salt.  Any corrections are welcome.)

Ps. If you run quickly back down to the level where the trap was, your
pet worm may still be tame, especially if it was well fed (which I
suppose a purple worm is likely to be).

